From: Frederic Weisbecker <fweisbecker@suse.com>
Subject: kABI workaround for CPUHP_AP_KTHREADS_ONLINE
Patch-mainline: Never, kABI workaround
References: bsc#1269313

The backport of:

        d1a89197589c ("kthread: Default affine kthread to its preferred NUMA node")

introduced CPUHP_AP_KTHREADS_ONLINE, which changes the position of
some cpuhotplug states used by modules, such as CPUHP_AP_ONLINE_DYN
for example. But kthreads hotplug handler can safely be called
dynamically at the end of the online process.

Signed-off-by: Frederic Weisbecker <fweisbecker@suse.com>
Reviewed-by: Petr Pavlu <petr.pavlu@suse.com>
---
 include/linux/cpuhotplug.h |    1 -
 kernel/kthread.c           |    2 +-
 2 files changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/include/linux/cpuhotplug.h
+++ b/include/linux/cpuhotplug.h
@@ -249,7 +249,6 @@ enum cpuhp_state {
 	CPUHP_AP_WORKQUEUE_ONLINE,
 	CPUHP_AP_RANDOM_ONLINE,
 	CPUHP_AP_RCUTREE_ONLINE,
-	CPUHP_AP_KTHREADS_ONLINE,
 	CPUHP_AP_BASE_CACHEINFO_ONLINE,
 	CPUHP_AP_ONLINE_DYN,
 	CPUHP_AP_ONLINE_DYN_END		= CPUHP_AP_ONLINE_DYN + 40,
--- a/kernel/kthread.c
+++ b/kernel/kthread.c
@@ -862,7 +862,7 @@ static int kthreads_online_cpu(unsigned
 
 static int kthreads_init(void)
 {
-	return cpuhp_setup_state(CPUHP_AP_KTHREADS_ONLINE, "kthreads:online",
+	return cpuhp_setup_state(CPUHP_AP_ONLINE_DYN, "kthreads:online",
 				kthreads_online_cpu, NULL);
 }
 early_initcall(kthreads_init);
